  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0211, and it contains three tables: project, consultant, and service_record. The project table has five columns: Client_Name, End_Date, Name, Project_ID, and Start_Date. The Client_Name and Name columns are strings, and the End_Date, Start_Date, and Project_ID columns are integers. The Project_ID column is the primary key, and the Start_Date column has a default value of the current date and time. The consultant table has six columns: Consultant_ID, Date_of_Birth, Gender, Name, Phone_Number, and Professional_Field. The Consultant_ID column is the primary key, and the Date_of_Birth, Gender, Name, Phone_Number, and Professional_Field columns are strings. The service_record table has six columns: Consultant_ID, Project_ID, Service_Content, Service_Date, Service_ID, and FOREIGN KEY (Consultant_ID) REFERENCES consultant(Consultant_ID), FOREIGN KEY (Project_ID) REFERENCES project(Project_ID). The Consultant_ID and Project_ID columns are integers, and the Service_Content and Service_Date columns are strings. The Service_ID column is the primary key, and the FOREIGN KEY constraints ensure that the Consultant_ID and Project_ID columns reference the corresponding columns in the consultant and project tables, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "Consulting Service System Business Requirement Description:\nThe Technical Consulting Department provides multiple technical consulting service projects, each of which involves multiple consultants. Consulting service projects have a Project ID, Name, Start Date, End Date, and Client Name. Consultants have a Consultant ID, Name, Date of Birth, Gender, Phone Number, and Professional Field. Consulting service records need to record the Service ID, Project ID, Consultant ID, Service Date, and Service Content.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0211.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0211\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `Project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Client_Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Start_Date` datetime DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `End_Date` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Project_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `consultant` (\n  `Consultant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Date_of_Birth` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Gender` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Phone_Number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Professional_Field` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Consultant_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_record` (\n  `Service_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Consultant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Service_Content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Service_Date` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Service_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Consultant_ID`) REFERENCES `consultant` (`Consultant_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `service_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Project_ID`) REFERENCES `project` (`Project_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
